{\rtf1\ansi\deff0{\fonttbl{\f0 Times New Roman;}{\f1 Courier New;}}{\colortbl;\red32\green45\blue70;\red92\green77\blue212;}\paperw11906\paperh16838\margl1440\margr1440\margt1260\margb1260\widowctrl\viewkind4{\header{\pard\qr\fs18 ResumeIntel | Copyright submission\par}}{\footer{\pard\qc\fs18 Page \chpgn\par}}{\pard\fs34\b\qc\sb300\sa220 COMPLETE COPYRIGHT DOCUMENTATION\par}{\pard\fs22\qc\sa300 Technical description, architecture, methodology, verification and limitations\par}\page {\pard\fs26\b\sb360\sa160 1. Project background\par}{\pard\fs24\sa140\sl276\slmult1 ResumeIntel is an authenticated web application for evidence-grounded comparison of resume text with a target job description. It is positioned as decision support and reproducible research, not as an employer ATS, hiring predictor, or verified skills assessment.\par}{\pard\fs26\b\sb360\sa160 2. Problem statement and objectives\par}{\pard\fs24\sa140\sl276\slmult1 Keyword overlap can obscure context: a term listed without work evidence, a requirement not found, or a requirement outside the supported taxonomy can all be treated as equivalent by simpler systems. ResumeIntel\u8217?s objective is to make these distinctions inspectable, provide a transparent weighted coverage calculation, and persist the resulting report for review.\par}{\pard\fs26\b\sb360\sa160 3. System description and functional modules\par}\trowd\trgaph108\trleft0\trkeep
